            <ArticleTitle>Stent fracture: an unusual cause of late restenosis after sirolimus-eluting stent placement.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>988-91</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Stent fracture is uncommon but may have consequences including restenosis. To date, stent fractures reported have been related to aggressive post dilation. We describe a case that involves fracture of a stent deployed to nominal pressure. Unlike most stent fractures reported that involve stent struts only our case demonstrated circumferential disruption with complete separation of the stent segments.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
